  "source_facts": [
    "43d150 aux04 is separate from primary/transient/side icons. Source mode-change byte body2ec and primary100 determine create/rebuild/remove/retain; allocation43e210 has action0/facing0/priority10/flags20. Creation jumps directly to43d5a2 without animating or submitting that frame.",
    "When mode15 is1 or2 creation selects body2e8; otherwise literal103100 (192bc). Dirty2ec is set by C0 when prior body2e8 differs from raw incoming value16, not merely when mode15 changes; a fresh zeroed body resets mode15/value16/child state.",
    "Without dirty rebuild, primary100 absent removes an existing child. With leader100, missing child creates unless primary400+4000 are both set and8000 absent. Existing child with400 set removes; otherwise it advances and draws. Preserve native alternating create/remove cases rather than smoothing them.",
    "On a retained badge, copy unshifted parent screen and world position to child, run helper once, then query CURRENT child offsets/origins. Queued signed-short anchor is parentX+offsetX-originX and parentY+source body height+offsetY-originY. NULL style means palette0/flags0/colorffffffff, even if animation frame style differs. It precedes the other type1 child submissions and shares1024 slots.",
    "467060 toggles party at a strict unsigned (lastShortcutTick+500 modulo32)<now gate, sharing native global614884. Join uses facing0..7 to offset current local display by table53d4d4 and requires43f2d0 target: active indexed body, matching body DISPLAY, recordTypeFlags&28 nonzero and primary400 clear; local primary100 must also be clear. Leave skips facing/neighbor/own-leader checks. Both require input/movement/coordination guards clear.",
    "Producer4f77d0 sends exactly three int32 fields with tag*Cc: current local displayX/displayY and join1 or leave0. No optimistic membership/mode mutation occurs in467060. Native614884 is in PE .data zero-fill tail; Ghidra initialized-memory read is00000000 and there is no authoritative original file mapping for that virtual address.",
    "Kk0/receive-00567cc0 calls4f3310 with mode/result. Mode1/result1 ORs local member200 without changing party mode. Mode0/result1 clears local200, sets party mode0, calls500500 (owned rows/queues and force/leader removal), then4f8340 sends /Re with local TARGET X/Y and sign-extended low byte of native facingf536ac. Other combinations do not change membership/mode; native pending wordf5f16c clears in the ordinary gate0 path.",
    "Current shared/session/client byte codecs already know *Cc, Kk0 and /Re descriptors. The new path must use those exact operations and the actual session queue, preserve request order and late-close cleanup, and retain ordinary party source ownership from stage178."
  ],
